      "body": "## Purpose\n\nA text-only deployment of a Pixtral-based model fails at engine init when it is also a KV/EC consumer: `--limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":0}'` together with a consumer `--kv-transfer-config` (`kv_consumer` or `kv_both`, e.g. a NixlConnector P/D decode worker or OffloadingConnector):\n\n```\nvllm.exceptions.VLLMValidationError: At most 0 image(s) may be provided in one prompt. (parameter=image)\n```\n\n*Root cause:* `_resolve_mm_embedding_inputs` enables `enable_mm_embeds` on every EC/KV consumer. With all limits at 0 that turns multimodal inputs back on (`supports_multimodal_inputs` is True whenever `enable_mm_embeds` is), the `MultiModalBudget` then sizes the image modality, and Pixtral's `get_dummy_inputs` builds one dummy image, which the limit of 0 rejects. A text-only deployment is never sent embeddings, so the resolution is now skipped there.\n\n`--language-model-only` also sets every limit to 0, but an EC consumer started with it skips the encoder and still receives embeddings from the EC connector, so it keeps `enable_mm_embeds=True` (second commit).\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```bash\npytest -q tests/config/test_multimodal_config.py\n\n# End to end: Pixtral (Mistral format), text-only, KV consumer.\n# load_format=\"dummy\", so only params.json + tekken.json are needed.\npython repro_textonly.py <pixtral_model_dir> offloading   # OffloadingConnector, kv_both\npython repro_textonly.py <pixtral_model_dir> nixl         # NixlConnector, kv_consumer\n```\n\n<details><summary>repro_textonly.py</summary>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\nfrom vllm import LLM, SamplingParams\n\nmodel, connector = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\nkv_transfer_config = {\n    \"offloading\": {\n        \"kv_connector\": \"OffloadingConnector\",\n        \"kv_role\": \"kv_both\",\n        \"kv_connector_extra_config\": {\"cpu_bytes_to_use\": 1 << 30},\n    },\n    \"nixl\": {\"kv_connector\": \"NixlConnector\", \"kv_role\": \"kv_consumer\"},\n}[connector]\n\nllm = LLM(\n    model=model,\n    tokenizer_mode=\"mistral\",\n    config_format=\"mistral\",\n    load_format=\"dummy\",\n    limit_mm_per_prompt={\"image\": 0},\n    kv_transfer_config=kv_transfer_config,\n    max_model_len=4096,\n    gpu_memory_utilization=0.3,\n    enforce_eager=True,\n)\nout = llm.generate([\"The capital of France is\"], SamplingParams(max_tokens=8))\nprint(\"OK text request:\", out[0].outputs[0].token_ids)\n```\n\n</details>\n\nRun on 1x GB300. The model was a 2-layer Pixtral config (Mistral format, `vision_encoder` section) with the Magistral-Small-2509 `tekken.json`.\n\n## Test Result\n\n| Check | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Text-only Pixtral + OffloadingConnector `kv_both` | engine init fails: `VLLMValidationError: At most 0 image(s) ...` | starts, `enable_mm_embeds=False`, text request OK |\n| Text-only Pixtral + NixlConnector `kv_consumer` | engine init fails: same error | starts, text request OK |\n| Pixtral `kv_consumer` with images allowed, or `image:0` plus `--enable-mm-embeds` | `enable_mm_embeds=True` | unchanged (`True`) |\n| Pixtral `ec_consumer` + `--language-model-only` | `enable_mm_embeds=True` | unchanged (`True`) |\n| new `test_text_only_consumer_stays_text_only` | 2 failed (kv/ec consumer with all limits 0 enable embeds) | 3 passed |\n| `tests/config/test_multimodal_config.py` | 87 passed | 90 passed |\n\nAI assistance was used for this change.\n",
